.SS ctrl-\e menu popup
/ starts a Sessions filter, also from Commands. Type to match label or engine
ignoring case; backspace edits. Enter ends editing and keeps matching rows;
Enter again keeps the selected session. Esc clears the filter; another Esc
goes back. While editing, printable keys enter text. Afterwards hotkeys
act on all rows, including hidden windows.
.PP
Sessions opens with the current session selected. With no sessions, Commands opens
and Sessions says "no sessions yet". tab and shift+tab switch Sessions / Commands.
Commands groups keys under start and open, the session's agent, panes, and leave,
and shows "for #<n> <name>" for the session selected on Sessions.
Arrows preview on Sessions and move without preview on Commands. Enter keeps the
session on Sessions and runs the command on Commands. Hotkeys work in either tab.


