.SS Loops board

Board is the default tab. Tab and shift-Tab switch to Contractors (N), counting
running and unseen finished agents. Use ↑↓/jk to select, ⏎ for full output,
esc to return or close, and q to close. Opening finished output marks it seen.
Running builders, reviewers and arbiters precede finished agents: unseen first,
then seen within 24 hours, newest first. At 100 columns or wider live output
appears beside the list; PgUp/PgDn scroll it and G resumes following the end.
Below 100 columns use ⏎ for output.


Loops is a popup; \fBptln loop tab\fR runs the same board full-screen. Add \fB--contractor <id>\fR to open its Contractors tab with that contractor selected; an unknown or malformed id selects the first contractor.
Five columns show needs you, then planned, in progress, in review and done.
Below 110 columns, three columns are visible.
With bare \fBptln\fR, a new server starts the saved workspace, or a shell in the
current directory if none exists, then opens the launcher popup. Existing servers
keep their focus. Obsolete permanent Loops and launcher windows are closed on start or attach.

