.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PARTYLINE_MEMORY_REFRESH=off
Do not show new facts during a session.
.TP
.B PARTYLINE_MEMORY_CAPTURE=off
Do not record facts from a session's work.
.TP
.B PARTYLINE_ENGINE
The engine \fBN\fR starts: claude, codex, gemini or antigravity. Default claude.
.TP
.B PARTYLINE_TMUX_SOCKET
The tmux socket name. Default \fBpartyline\fR.
.TP
.B PARTYLINE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 \fRor\fB NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER=1
Do not check for a newer version.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the session manager:
.PP
.nf
    ptln
.fi
.PP
Start Claude in a new worktree:
.PP
.nf
    ptln new claude \-\-worktree spike\-auth
.fi
.PP
Set up memory in a repository, then review and commit it:
.PP
.nf
    ptln memory build             # what it would write
    ptln memory build \-\-apply
    git status memory/ AGENTS.md
.fi
.PP
Record a fact, then correct it:
.PP
.nf
    ptln memory add gotcha "The importer rejects CSV files with a byte-order mark."
    ptln memory edit 20261017\-2013 "The importer strips a byte-order mark since v2.4."
.fi
.PP
Open the chat with the sessions in tabs 10 and 11:
.PP
.nf
    ptln chat
    /add 10 11
.fi
